Menagerie derives the robot description and meshes from Franka Emika:
https://github.com/frankaemika/franka_ros/tree/develop/franka_description

The original panda.xml, all visual/collision meshes and Apache-2.0 LICENSE
are preserved unchanged here. provenance.json records their source and hashes.

ESRB composes this model into ../tool_handling.xml. Scene adaptations:
- namespace materials, mesh names and default classes;
- mount the fixed base on the workbench and add an end-effector frame;
- enable body gravity compensation; keep the seven joint masses, inertias,
  limits, arm position servos and actuator force limits;
- preserve native finger joints and their tendon/equality coupling, with a
  700 N/m, 5 N*s/m gripper servo, 20 N tendon force limit and opening slew limit;
- apply ESR contact solver/friction settings and record robot collisions.

Actions are seven joint target angles plus a grip closure command. Motion
is generated by articulated joint dynamics. A damped Jacobian solver produces
joint targets from task waypoints; no gripper/tool pose is assigned after reset.
